#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Unit vectors for rekha's point instructions, generated by FreeType itself (rekha 0.8.1).

    python3 scripts/hint_unit_vectors.py emit programs/hint_unit_vectors.cyr
    python3 scripts/hint_unit_vectors.py list               # every program and what it proves
    python3 scripts/hint_unit_vectors.py dump <program>     # the points before and after, per point

WHY THIS EXISTS. programs/hint_test.cyr checks rekha's interpreter against numbers a second
hand-written interpreter produced, and two interpreters written from the same spec share the
same misreadings. This script builds a synthetic TrueType font — one simple glyph of two contours
carrying a test PROGRAM — hands it to the installed FreeType through scripts/ftshim.py (classic
interpreter, version 35, NO_AUTOHINT), and records what FreeType's glyph slot holds afterwards:
every outline point's hinted position, its tag byte with the touch bits, and the advance. Those
are the expected values; nothing here computes what an instruction SHOULD do.

THE PROGRAM LIST is written against the coverage spec of the 0.8.1 design (§4 K and amendment
A11): every point instruction and every opcode variant; every operand's zone read through a mixed
zp0/zp1/zp2 assignment where swapping two zones changes the answer; SLOOP counts popped from the
TOP of the stack (a fourth pushed value stays for the next instruction); moves whose freedom
vector is not the projection vector (perpendicular, near-perpendicular, anti-parallel, the 3:4
diagonal, the prenormalised-length-over-0x10000 diagonal, the F_dot_P = 0x3FFE edge, the X-only
and Y-only fast paths of SFVFS 236 1 / 1 236, a near-vertical SPVTL whose SHP touches without
moving); MIAP/MIRP cut-in with and without the opcode bit in the glyph zone, and cut-in and
auto-flip in the twilight zone with a freedom vector that lets them fire; MDRP/MD[1]/IP reading
orus (font units) rather than org at scale 0.75, on coordinates whose residues mod 4 make the two
disagree; MDRP rounding under RTHG and SROUND; SDPVTL after MDAP[1] moved an endpoint; ISECT
crossing, grazing and parallel; ALIGNPTS halving 3/64 toward zero; SHC's reference-point exclusion
both ways; SHZ excluding the phantom points and touching nothing; FLIP* on the glyph zone while
every zp is twilight; DELTAP1/2/3 match, no match, SDB, SDS and a ppem band out of range;
twilight results read out into glyph points; UTP under each freedom vector; rp0/rp1/rp2 made
observable by the instruction that reads them next. IUP and composite glyphs are excluded
(0.8.2's).

THE 0.8.1 VERIFICATION ROUND added the rows its reviewers probed FreeType with: the projection
fast path (Compute_Funcs selects Project_x whenever projVector.x is EXACTLY 0x4000, whatever
the y component holds, and Project_y likewise — ref2143/ttinterp.c:2281-2293 — and Normalize
hands back such a vector for SPVFS 236 1 and for the outline's own near-axis edges through
SPVTL), the same rule on the dual vector, the single-width sign restore with a negative SSW and
in its negative-distance branch, the strict single-width window, every rounding state through
MDRP's round bit, a zero original distance under minimum distance and auto-flip, MSIRP's
original-position move into twilight on its general, X-only and Y-only paths, MIAP/MDRP/MIRP
into twilight under a perpendicular or anti-parallel freedom vector, the MIRP cut-in's same-zone
gate, SxVTL/SDPVTL operand zones, SPVFS on (0, 0) and on a value above 16 bits, the 16-bit
truncation FreeType applies to SDB's operand and to point, reference-point and contour operands
(an FT_UShort cast before the bounds test, so 65536 + k names k in BOTH FreeType modes), a
forward jump past the end of a program, LOOPCALL with a negative count, an IF left open at the
end, a font-defined IDEF for opcode 0x91 on a static face, IDEFs of four unassigned opcodes and
of a standard one, function numbers above maxFunctionDefs, FreeType's floor of 64 on the
definition count, and GETINFO's grayscale bit as an fpgm sees it (0) against a glyph program (on).

FONT VARIANTS. Every font here has the same outline, phantoms and cvt; a variant may differ from
font 0 in its `prep`, its `fpgm` and/or one `maxp` field, and the module's header states per
font exactly which. Font 0 (prep RTG, the two-function fpgm, the default maxp) carries every
program that is not about a table. Fonts 1..3 have preps that set graphics-state fields
(SMD/SCVTCI/SDB/SDS), rewrite a cvt entry (WCVTF) and DELTAC one, and their programs read the
carry-over out of the glyph program — the evidence, from FreeType itself, of what a prep run
leaves behind for a glyph. Fonts 4..6 define instructions in their prep; fonts 7..9 replace the
fpgm (sparse function numbers, a function defined conditionally on GETINFO at fpgm time) and two
of them lower maxp.maxFunctionDefs. No prep is empty: FreeType keeps a stale graphics state for a
font without one, and that quirk must never reach this module.

EVERY PROGRAM IS ALSO LOADED UNDER FT_LOAD_PEDANTIC on a fresh face and must load with rc 0. That
is the proof that FreeType skipped nothing silently — a bad point index, a short stack, an
out-of-range cvt entry all fail the load in pedantic mode and pass it in the default mode with the
instruction dropped. A program that fails pedantic is a bug in the program. No program moves pp1
(the x origin of the reported outline) and the loops stay far below FreeType's per-run limits.

WHERE THE NON-DEGENERACY CHECKS COME FROM. For the rows whose whole point is a 1/64 disagreement
between two readings (orus vs org, fast path vs general, prenormalised length, the orthogonal
regime, a prep carry-over) this script also computes what the WRONG reading would give and asserts
FreeType's answer differs from it. Those small helpers (mulfix, muldiv, a port of
FT_Vector_NormLen, the per-row models of one instruction under a chosen projection) exist only
to prove each such row can fail; they never produce an expected value. Every row added by the
verification round carries such a check. Every program on a font variant is also run on font 0
and must answer differently there, or fail to load there, unless its point is that the variant
changes nothing (the IDEF of a standard opcode).

THE EMITTER CHECKS ITS OWN OUTPUT before writing it: no line over 120 bytes, none of cyrlint's
deferral words, `cyrius lint --strict` with zero warn/deferral lines, and `cyrius fmt` on a copy
that must come back byte-identical. Any failure leaves the destination untouched.

NOT RUN IN CI. CI's Ubuntu ships FreeType 2.13.2, whose move arithmetic, ODD/EVEN, stack margin
and DELTAP pops differ from the 2.14.3 rekha targets; the committed module is regenerated by hand
on a 2.14.x host and reviewed like any other transcription. Python 3 stdlib only.
"""
import os
import shutil
import struct
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
import ftshim  # noqa: E402

UPEM = 1024
ADVANCE = 600
ASCENDER = 800
DESCENDER = -200

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The glyph: two contours, fourteen points, on- and off-curve mixed, no coordinate on a multiple
# of four so that scale 0.75 (12 ppem) rounds every one of them. Phantom points follow as 14..17.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OUTLINE = [
    (101, 5, 1),
    (199, 2, 0),
    (407, 6, 1),
    (503, 102, 0),
    (498, 301, 1),
    (405, 406, 0),
    (207, 398, 1),
    (98, 203, 0),
    (201, 101, 1),
    (302, 97, 1),
    (303, 199, 0),
    (299, 302, 1),
    (198, 297, 0),
    (150, 203, 1),
]
CONTOUR_ENDS = [7, 13]
NPTS = len(OUTLINE)
PP1, PP2, PP3, PP4 = NPTS, NPTS + 1, NPTS + 2, NPTS + 3

XMIN = min(p[0] for p in OUTLINE)
XMAX = max(p[0] for p in OUTLINE)
YMIN = min(p[1] for p in OUTLINE)
YMAX = max(p[1] for p in OUTLINE)
LSB = XMIN  # lsb == xMin puts pp1 at x = 0 (ref2143/ttgload.c tt_loader_set_pp)


def phantoms():
    """The four phantom points in FONT UNITS, exactly as ref2143/ttgload.c:1336-1347
    (tt_loader_set_pp) computes them for a font WITHOUT a `vmtx` table and WITHOUT `OS/2`:
    pp1 = (xMin - lsb, 0), pp2 = (pp1.x + advance, 0); TT_Get_VMetrics (ttgload.c:112-138) then
    gives tsb = hhea.Ascender - yMax and ah = |Ascender - Descender|, so pp3 = (0, yMax + tsb) =
    (0, Ascender) and pp4 = (0, pp3.y - ah) = (0, Descender). pp3.x/pp4.x stay 0 in the classic
    interpreter (the advance/2 form is version 40 only)."""
    pp1 = (XMIN - LSB, 0)
    pp2 = (pp1[0] + ADVANCE, 0)
    tsb = ASCENDER - YMAX
    ah = abs(ASCENDER - DESCENDER)
    pp3 = (0, YMAX + tsb)
    pp4 = (0, pp3[1] - ah)
    return [pp1, pp2, pp3, pp4]


def cvt_entry(i):
    """programs/hint_test.cyr's synthetic cvt: i * 101 - 505, entry 5 exactly 0."""
    return i * 101 - 505


CVT = [cvt_entry(i) for i in range(16)]

# fpgm of font 0: function 3 adds 5, function 7 adds 1 (programs/hint_test.cyr's build_syn).
# Assembled by asm() below, byte for byte B0 03 2C B0 05 60 2D B0 07 2C B0 01 60 2D.
FPGM_TEXT = "PUSHB 3 FDEF PUSHB 5 ADD ENDF PUSHB 7 FDEF PUSHB 1 ADD ENDF"

# maxp of font 0; a variant may override one field by name.
MAX_TWILIGHT = 16
MAX_STORAGE = 32
MAX_STACK = 128
MAXP_DEFAULT = {"maxFunctionDefs": 64, "maxInstructionDefs": 4}


def font(name, prep, why, fpgm=None, maxp=None):
    """A font VARIANT: `prep` is its control-value program (assembled, never empty), `fpgm` its
    font program when it is not font 0's, `maxp` the maxp fields it overrides."""
    return {"name": name, "prep": prep, "why": why, "fpgm": fpgm, "maxp": maxp or {}}


# The font VARIANTS: same outline, phantoms and cvt; font 0 is the one every program not about a
# table runs on, and each other font differs from it in its prep, its fpgm and/or one maxp field.
FONTS = [
    font("rtg", "RTG",
         "the default round state restated; every program not about a table runs under it"),
    font("gs_carry", "PUSHB 96 SMD PUSHB 40 SCVTCI PUSHB 10 SDB PUSHB 4 SDS",
         "four of the graphics-state fields FreeType keeps from a prep for every glyph program"),
    font("wcvtf", "PUSHB 8 PUSHW 400 WCVTF",
         "cvt 8 becomes 400 font units (300 at 12 ppem) for the size"),
    font("deltac", "PUSHB 63 8 1 DELTAC1",
         "cvt 8 gains 8 steps of 1/8 px at 12 ppem (band 3 of base 9) and nothing at 28"),
    font("idef_91", "RTG PUSHB 145 IDEF PUSHB 64 SHPIX ENDF",
         "prep defines opcode 0x91 (GETVARIATION on a variation face) as SHPIX 64: on a static face "
         "FreeType runs the IDEF (ref2143/ttinterp.c:7306-7314; LaoUI.ttf does this)"),
    font("idef_four", "RTG PUSHB 40 IDEF PUSHB 64 SHPIX ENDF PUSHB 123 IDEF PUSHB 32 SHPIX ENDF "
         "PUSHB 143 IDEF PUSHB 16 SHPIX ENDF PUSHB 160 IDEF PUSHB 8 SHPIX ENDF",
         "prep defines the unassigned opcodes 0x28, 0x7B, 0x8F and 0xA0 (all four maxInstructionDefs "
         "slots) as SHPIX by 64, 32, 16 and 8"),
    font("idef_std", "RTG PUSHB 96 IDEF PUSHB 64 SHPIX ENDF",
         "prep IDEFs 0x60 (ADD): a standard instruction is dispatched before the IDEF table is looked "
         "at, so the definition is never reached"),
    font("fdef_sparse", "RTG",
         "fpgm REPLACED: functions 0 (SHPIX 32), 1 (SHPIX 16) and 100 (SHPIX 64) with "
         "maxp.maxFunctionDefs 3 — FreeType bounds the COUNT of definitions, not the numbers "
         "(ref2143/ttinterp.c:3283-3309)",
         fpgm="PUSHB 0 FDEF PUSHB 32 SHPIX ENDF PUSHB 1 FDEF PUSHB 16 SHPIX ENDF "
              "PUSHB 100 FDEF PUSHB 64 SHPIX ENDF",
         maxp={"maxFunctionDefs": 3}),
    font("fpgm_getinfo", "RTG",
         "fpgm EXTENDED: function 9 is defined under IF on GETINFO's grayscale bit AT FPGM TIME "
         "(SHPIX 128 when set, 64 when clear) and function 10 answers GETINFO 32 when called",
         fpgm=FPGM_TEXT + " PUSHB 32 GETINFO IF PUSHB 9 FDEF PUSHB 128 SHPIX ENDF ELSE "
              "PUSHB 9 FDEF PUSHB 64 SHPIX ENDF EIF PUSHB 10 FDEF PUSHB 32 GETINFO ENDF"),
    font("fdef_floor", "RTG",
         "fpgm REPLACED: functions 5 (SHPIX 64) and 9 (SHPIX 32) with maxp.maxFunctionDefs 1 — "
         "FreeType's maxp loader floors maxFunctionDefs at 64 (measured on 2.14.3: 64 definitions "
         "load under a declared 1, 65 fail), so two definitions fit",
         fpgm="PUSHB 5 FDEF PUSHB 64 SHPIX ENDF PUSHB 9 FDEF PUSHB 32 SHPIX ENDF",
         maxp={"maxFunctionDefs": 1}),
]


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A small assembler, so every program below reads as TrueType and the module can carry the text.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPS = {
    "SVTCA[y]": 0x00, "SVTCA[x]": 0x01, "SPVTCA[y]": 0x02, "SPVTCA[x]": 0x03,
    "SFVTCA[y]": 0x04, "SFVTCA[x]": 0x05, "SPVTL[0]": 0x06, "SPVTL[1]": 0x07,
    "SFVTL[0]": 0x08, "SFVTL[1]": 0x09, "SPVFS": 0x0A, "SFVFS": 0x0B, "GPV": 0x0C, "GFV": 0x0D,
    "SFVTPV": 0x0E, "ISECT": 0x0F, "SRP0": 0x10, "SRP1": 0x11, "SRP2": 0x12, "SZP0": 0x13,
    "SZP1": 0x14, "SZP2": 0x15, "SZPS": 0x16, "SLOOP": 0x17, "RTG": 0x18, "RTHG": 0x19,
    "SMD": 0x1A, "SCVTCI": 0x1D, "SSWCI": 0x1E, "SSW": 0x1F, "DUP": 0x20, "POP": 0x21,
    "CLEAR": 0x22, "SWAP": 0x23, "DEPTH": 0x24, "CINDEX": 0x25, "MINDEX": 0x26, "ALIGNPTS": 0x27,
    "UTP": 0x29, "CALL": 0x2B, "MDAP[0]": 0x2E, "MDAP[1]": 0x2F, "SHP[0]": 0x32, "SHP[1]": 0x33,
    "SHC[0]": 0x34, "SHC[1]": 0x35, "SHZ[0]": 0x36, "SHZ[1]": 0x37, "SHPIX": 0x38, "IP": 0x39,
    "MSIRP[0]": 0x3A, "MSIRP[1]": 0x3B, "ALIGNRP": 0x3C, "RTDG": 0x3D, "MIAP[0]": 0x3E,
    "MIAP[1]": 0x3F, "WS": 0x42, "RS": 0x43, "WCVTP": 0x44, "RCVT": 0x45, "GC[0]": 0x46,
    "GC[1]": 0x47, "SCFS": 0x48, "MD[0]": 0x49, "MD[1]": 0x4A, "MPPEM": 0x4B, "FLIPON": 0x4D,
    "FLIPOFF": 0x4E, "DELTAP1": 0x5D, "SDB": 0x5E, "SDS": 0x5F, "ADD": 0x60, "SUB": 0x61,
    "NEG": 0x65, "ROUND[0]": 0x68, "WCVTF": 0x70, "DELTAP2": 0x71, "DELTAP3": 0x72,
    "DELTAC1": 0x73, "DELTAC2": 0x74, "DELTAC3": 0x75, "SROUND": 0x76, "S45ROUND": 0x77,
    "ROFF": 0x7A, "RUTG": 0x7C, "RDTG": 0x7D, "FLIPPT": 0x80, "FLIPRGON": 0x81, "FLIPRGOFF": 0x82,
    "SDPVTL[0]": 0x86, "SDPVTL[1]": 0x87, "ROLL": 0x8A,
    "JMPR": 0x1C, "ELSE": 0x1B, "LOOPCALL": 0x2A, "FDEF": 0x2C, "ENDF": 0x2D, "IF": 0x58,
    "EIF": 0x59, "GETINFO": 0x88, "IDEF": 0x89,
}
for _v in range(32):
    OPS["MDRP[%s]" % format(_v, "05b")] = 0xC0 + _v
    OPS["MIRP[%s]" % format(_v, "05b")] = 0xE0 + _v
NAMES = dict((v, k) for k, v in OPS.items())


def asm(text):
    """Assemble `text`. Tokens are mnemonics from OPS; `PUSHB a b c` / `PUSHW a b c` take their
    operands from the following integer tokens (NPUSHB/NPUSHW when there are more than 8); a
    two-digit `0xNN` is never an operand but that opcode byte itself (the unassigned ones an IDEF
    defines, and 0x91), which is how disasm() spells an opcode it has no name for."""
    out = bytearray()
    toks = text.replace("\n", " ").replace(";", " ").split()
    i = 0
    while i < len(toks):
        t = toks[i]
        i += 1
        if _is_raw_opcode(t):
            out.append(int(t, 16))
        elif t in ("PUSHB", "PUSHW"):
            vals = []
            while i < len(toks) and _is_int(toks[i]) and not _is_raw_opcode(toks[i]) and len(vals) < 255:
                vals.append(int(toks[i], 0))
                i += 1
            assert vals, "empty %s" % t
            if t == "PUSHB":
                assert all(0 <= v <= 255 for v in vals), vals
                if len(vals) > 8:
                    out += bytes([0x40, len(vals)])
                else:
                    out.append(0xB0 + len(vals) - 1)
                out += bytes(vals)
            else:
                assert all(-32768 <= v <= 32767 for v in vals), vals
                if len(vals) > 8:
                    out += bytes([0x41, len(vals)])
                else:
                    out.append(0xB8 + len(vals) - 1)
                for v in vals:
                    out += struct.pack(">h", v)
        else:
            assert t in OPS, "unknown mnemonic %r" % t
            out.append(OPS[t])
    return bytes(out)


def _is_int(t):
    try:
        int(t, 0)
        return True
    except ValueError:
        return False


def _is_raw_opcode(t):
    return len(t) == 4 and t.startswith("0x") and _is_int(t) and t not in OPS


def disasm(code):
    """One line of mnemonics per instruction, for the module's comments and `dump`."""
    out, ip = [], 0
    while ip < len(code):
        op = code[ip]
        if 0xB0 <= op <= 0xB7 or op == 0x40:
            n, ip = (op - 0xB0 + 1, ip) if op != 0x40 else (code[ip + 1], ip + 1)
            out.append("PUSHB " + " ".join(str(b) for b in code[ip + 1 : ip + 1 + n]))
            ip += 1 + n
        elif 0xB8 <= op <= 0xBF or op == 0x41:
            n, ip = (op - 0xB8 + 1, ip) if op != 0x41 else (code[ip + 1], ip + 1)
            vals = [struct.unpack(">h", code[ip + 1 + 2 * k : ip + 3 + 2 * k])[0] for k in range(n)]
            out.append("PUSHW " + " ".join(str(v) for v in vals))
            ip += 1 + 2 * n
        else:
            out.append(NAMES.get(op, "0x%02X" % op))
            ip += 1
    return out


# Twilight readouts: GC[0] on twilight point `t` (zp2 = 0), then SCFS glyph point `g` (zp2 = 1) to
# that value. The glyph point's projection becomes the twilight point's, in whatever vector is set.
def read_twilight(t, g):
    return "PUSHB 0 SZP2 PUSHB %d GC[0] PUSHB 1 SZP2 PUSHB %d SWAP SCFS" % (t, g)


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The font
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
def _checksum(b):
    b = b + b"\0" * ((4 - len(b) % 4) % 4)
    return sum(struct.unpack(">%dI" % (len(b) // 4), b)) & 0xFFFFFFFF


def _pad4(b):
    return b + b"\0" * ((4 - len(b) % 4) % 4)


def glyf_table(program):
    g = struct.pack(">hhhhh", len(CONTOUR_ENDS), XMIN, YMIN, XMAX, YMAX)
    g += b"".join(struct.pack(">H", e) for e in CONTOUR_ENDS)
    g += struct.pack(">H", len(program)) + program
    g += bytes(p[2] for p in OUTLINE)  # flag byte: bit 0 on-curve, x and y as int16 deltas
    px = py = 0
    xs = ys = b""
    for x, y, _ in OUTLINE:
        xs += struct.pack(">h", x - px)
        ys += struct.pack(">h", y - py)
        px, py = x, y
    return _pad4(g + xs + ys)


def prep_bytes(f):
    """The assembled prep of font variant `f`; never empty."""
    b = asm(FONTS[f]["prep"])
    assert b, "font %d has an empty prep" % f
    return b


def fpgm_bytes(f):
    """The assembled fpgm of font variant `f`: font 0's unless the variant replaces it."""
    text = FONTS[f]["fpgm"]
    return asm(FPGM_TEXT if text is None else text)


def maxp_fields(f):
    """The maxp fields font variant `f` sets: the defaults, then its overrides (names checked)."""
    fields = dict(MAXP_DEFAULT)
    for k, v in FONTS[f]["maxp"].items():
        assert k in fields, "font %d overrides unknown maxp field %r" % (f, k)
        fields[k] = v
    return fields


def font_differs(f):
    """What font variant `f` changes against font 0, for the module's header: the prep always
    (stated as its listing), then 'fpgm' and each overridden maxp field."""
    parts = []
    if FONTS[f]["fpgm"] is not None:
        parts.append("fpgm")
    for k in sorted(FONTS[f]["maxp"]):
        parts.append("maxp.%s %d" % (k, FONTS[f]["maxp"][k]))
    return parts


def build_font(program, max_ins, font=0):
    """A complete TrueType font whose glyph 1 carries `program`; glyph 0 is empty. `max_ins` is
    maxp.maxSizeOfInstructions, the same for every font here so the fonts differ ONLY in the
    glyph's instruction bytes and, between variants, the prep, fpgm and overridden maxp fields."""
    prep = prep_bytes(font)
    fpgm = fpgm_bytes(font)
    mx = maxp_fields(font)
    glyf = glyf_table(program)
    loca = struct.pack(">HHH", 0, 0, len(glyf) // 2)
    n_glyphs = 2
    head = struct.pack(
        ">IIIIHHqqhhhhHHhhh",
        0x00010000, 0x00010000, 0, 0x5F0F3CF5, 0b1011, UPEM, 0, 0,
        XMIN, YMIN, XMAX, YMAX, 0, 8, 2, 0, 0,
    )
    hhea = struct.pack(
        ">IhhhHhhhhhhhhhhhH",
        0x00010000, ASCENDER, DESCENDER, 0, ADVANCE, 0, 0, XMAX, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, n_glyphs,
    )
    hmtx = struct.pack(">HhHh", ADVANCE, 0, ADVANCE, LSB)
    cvt = b"".join(struct.pack(">h", v) for v in CVT)
    assert len(program) <= max_ins, (len(program), max_ins)
    assert len(fpgm) <= max_ins and len(prep) <= max_ins, (font, len(fpgm), len(prep), max_ins)
    maxp = struct.pack(
        ">IHHHHHHHHHHHHHH",
        0x00010000, n_glyphs, NPTS, len(CONTOUR_ENDS), 0, 0, 2, MAX_TWILIGHT, MAX_STORAGE,
        mx["maxFunctionDefs"], mx["maxInstructionDefs"], MAX_STACK, max_ins, 0, 0,
    )
    sub = struct.pack(">HHH", 0, 262, 0) + bytes([1 if c == ord("A") else 0 for c in range(256)])
    cmap = struct.pack(">HH", 0, 1) + struct.pack(">HHI", 1, 0, 12) + sub
    post = struct.pack(">IIhhIIIII", 0x00030000, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)
    tables = {
        b"cmap": cmap, b"cvt ": cvt, b"fpgm": fpgm, b"glyf": glyf, b"head": head, b"hhea": hhea,
        b"hmtx": hmtx, b"loca": loca, b"maxp": maxp, b"post": post, b"prep": prep,
    }
    tags = sorted(tables)
    hdr = struct.pack(">IHHHH", 0x00010000, len(tags), 0, 0, 0)
    off = 12 + 16 * len(tags)
    dirs, body = b"", b""
    for t in tags:
        d = tables[t]
        dirs += struct.pack(">4sIII", t, _checksum(d), off + len(body), len(d))
        body += _pad4(d)
    return hdr + dirs + body


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Arithmetic helpers — ONLY for the non-degeneracy assertions (see the docstring).
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
def mulfix(a, b):
    s = 1
    if a < 0:
        a, s = -a, -s
    if b < 0:
        b, s = -b, -s
    c = (a * b + 0x8000) >> 16
    return c if s > 0 else -c


def muldiv(a, b, c):
    s = 1
    if a < 0:
        a, s = -a, -s
    if b < 0:
        b, s = -b, -s
    if c < 0:
        c, s = -c, -s
    d = (a * b + c // 2) // c if c else 0x7FFFFFFF
    return d if s > 0 else -d


def divfix(a, b):
    s = 1
    if a < 0:
        a, s = -a, -s
    if b < 0:
        b, s = -b, -s
    c = (a * 65536 + b // 2) // b
    return c if s > 0 else -c


def scale_for(ppem):
    return divfix(ppem * 64, UPEM)


def pix_round(v):
    return (v + 32) & ~63


def _s32(v):
    v &= 0xFFFFFFFF
    return v - (1 << 32) if v & 0x80000000 else v


def normlen(x_, y_):
    """A port of FT_Vector_NormLen (ref2143/ftcalc.c:786-874): (vx, vy) in 16.16 and the
    prenormalised length estimate `l` whose excess over 0x10000 makes the Newton step's `b`
    negative — the case D7 of the design needs a signed shift for."""
    sx, x = (-1, -x_) if x_ < 0 else (1, x_)
    sy, y = (-1, -y_) if y_ < 0 else (1, y_)
    if x == 0:
        return (0, sy * 0x10000 if y else 0, y)
    if y == 0:
        return (sx * 0x10000 if x else 0, 0, x)
    l = (x + (y >> 1)) if x > y else (y + (x >> 1))
    shift = 31 - (l.bit_length() - 1)
    shift -= 15 + (1 if l >= ((0xAAAAAAAA >> shift) & 0xFFFFFFFF) else 0)
    if shift > 0:
        x = (x << shift) & 0xFFFFFFFF
        y = (y << shift) & 0xFFFFFFFF
        l = (x + (y >> 1)) if x > y else (y + (x >> 1))
    else:
        x >>= -shift
        y >>= -shift
        l >>= -shift
    b = 0x10000 - _s32(l)
    xs, ys = _s32(x), _s32(y)
    while True:
        u = (xs + ((xs * b) >> 16)) & 0xFFFFFFFF
        v = (ys + ((ys * b) >> 16)) & 0xFFFFFFFF
        z = int(-_s32(u * u + v * v) / 0x200)
        z = int(z * ((0x10000 + b) >> 8) / 0x10000)
        b += z
        if z <= 0:
            break
    return (-u if sx < 0 else u, -v if sy < 0 else v, l)


def normalize(x, y):
    """Normalize (ref2143/ttinterp.c): F2Dot14 unit vector, C truncation of the 16.16 / 4."""
    vx, vy, l = normlen(x, y)
    return int(vx / 4), int(vy / 4), l


def dotfix14(dx, dy, ax, ay):
    v = dx * ax + dy * ay + 0x2000
    return v >> 14  # arithmetic shift (Python's >> is), the 64-bit form


def rtg(v):
    """Round_To_Grid with no compensation (ref2143/ttinterp.c): half away from zero."""
    return pix_round(v) if v >= 0 else 0 - pix_round(0 - v)


# The two readings of a projection, for the fast-path rows: `general` is TT_DotFix14 on both
# components; `fast` is what Compute_Funcs selects (ref2143/ttinterp.c:2281-2293) — dx alone when
# the vector's x is exactly 0x4000, dy alone when its y is, the dot product otherwise. The rows'
# checks run one model of the instruction under each and assert FreeType took the second.
def general(vx, vy, pv):
    return dotfix14(vx, vy, pv[0], pv[1])


def fast(vx, vy, pv):
    if pv[0] == 0x4000:
        return vx
    if pv[1] == 0x4000:
        return vy
    return general(vx, vy, pv)


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The programs. Each: name, ppem, source text, one line of what it proves, optional self-check.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROGRAMS = []


def program(name, ppem, proves, text, check=None, font=0):
    assert name not in [p["name"] for p in PROGRAMS], name
    assert 0 <= font < len(FONTS), (name, font)
    PROGRAMS.append(
        {"name": name, "ppem": ppem, "proves": proves, "text": text, "check": check, "font": font}
    )


